A||||5||My7Fieros||Fiero blues....2 of the daily drivers....wont start||||8||
Z||000000||My7Fieros||12-29-2000||07:41 PM||||Well the other day was simply horrible (and it hasnt gotten better yet)...<BR>First, I get in my Formula...the thing wont start. Itll crank, just wont start. Hmmm, Ill take a look at it on Saturday.<BR>So I get my stuff and move to the SE (86 V6 4 speed)..now this car is "ole reliable"..this car looks and runs like its brand new...80K miles!<BR>Well I go to crank her up and ...........nothing! No lights, no NOTHING! (SIGH)...well I ask my roommate about it (used to be his car) and he says that its something with the battery terminals...he says to take them off, check them, and put them back on...okay, whatever.<BR>So I take them off..they seem ok..put them back on, whammo! fires right up!<BR>Ok then...then, (now keep in mind that it hasnt gotten over roughly 30 degrees in the past month here) when I go to shift gears, it takes EVERY bit of strenghth Ive got! It does this for about the first 15 minutes of driving, then gets a good bit better (but still alittle too stiff for my taste).<BR>Well I go to leave work last night, start the car, nothing again..had to do the "terminal" thing again...<BR>Heres the thing, you can jiggle the battery and watch the trunk light come on and off...if it comes on..the minute I turn the key, everything goes dead again..I have to literaly disconnect the terminal wires and re-connect them to the batt...<B>W T F? </B><BR>To make matters worse, my girlfriend calls me that afternoon and tells me HER car wont start! THREE CARS IN THE SAME DAY?!!! <B>AAARRRGGGG!!! </B>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><BR>Well I fixed her car, but Im wondering whats wrong w/ the SE? Any ideas?<BR>Ill worry about the Formula next.......(sigh)...||||reg||8
Z||000001||Cooter||12-29-2000||08:30 PM||||All I can say is that you are lucky to have 5 more Fieros to pick from.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>It sounds like your battery is still not making good connection and when you disturb the connection, it will pass enough power to light up a few lights. A wire brush on the cables and terminals may cure it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||12-29-2000||11:10 PM||||Your shifting problem is likely the wrong oil in the tranny.<P>Repair/replace the battery cables and clean the terminals.<P>This is not at all common in very cold or very hot weather. The car needs more power to start under either condition.<P>On the formula you'll have to do the spark & fuel checks and all that. Also check the big harness connector by the battery. That has been known to get crappy contact and do things like this.||||reg||1
Z||000003||turbo86se||12-30-2000||01:47 AM||||Wow, sorry to hear about that! Reminds me when I had two alternators go bad in one day! One on my '88 coupe and one on my old '95 Altima! Al least the Fiero was a cheap fix! ||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroJoe||12-31-2000||06:18 PM||||baking soda and water will also dissolve battery corrosion, and can get into places where a wire brush may not be able to reach.<P>If you tighen the batter cables as tight as the can go, possibly the terminals in the battery, where the cables are recieved into, comes loose and the battery itself is at fault.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Cheever2||12-31-2000||07:17 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroJoe:<BR><B>baking soda and water will also dissolve battery corrosion...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE>I have seen 7-UP do the trick when baking soda was not available.<BR>I hope that's all the problem is.<P><P>------------------<BR><I>Chuck Hodges</I>||||reg||1
